# PART 03 — PRODUCT DESIGN PRINCIPLES

The system must follow these principles:

### 3.1 Single Source of Truth

Every major entity must have one authoritative record.

Examples:

- One customer record.
- One employee profile.
- One project record.
- One contract record.
- One financial transaction record.

Departments must use the same underlying records rather than creating separate copies.

### 3.2 Workflow-Based Architecture

The system must understand how work moves between departments.

Examples:

Sales → Contract → Project → Production → Review → Delivery → Finance.

### 3.3 Role-Based Experience

Different users must see different dashboards, navigation items, records and available actions according to their permissions.

### 3.4 Data Integrity

Do not allow operations that create inconsistent records, duplicate financial entries, broken relationships or unauthorized access.

### 3.5 Real Functionality

Every button, filter, form, table, page, menu item and action must work.

Do not create decorative buttons that do nothing.

Do not use static fake numbers as actual company metrics.

### 3.6 Maintainability

Separate the application into logical modules with clear responsibilities.

Do not put the entire application into one oversized component or one backend file.

### 3.7 Scalability

Design the foundation for future expansion to more branches, larger teams, more projects and more operational complexity.

